      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "tion it depends on the will of the writer. Rhetoricians, how-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ever, consider it a fault called ‘ विसंन्धिदोष ’ See Kàv. P. VII.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 3. अज्ञ—जानातीति ज्ञः ( ज्ञा+क ) न ज्ञः अज्ञः । सुखं, सुखतरं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "used as adverbs. विशेषं जानातीति विशेषज्ञः । ज्ञानलव०-लव m. is de-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "rived from लू to cut, to divide; a particle. दुर्विदग्ध-विदग्ध properly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "means what is well burnt, polished and burnished; hence refined",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "with culture, learned; दुष्टं यथा तथा विदग्धः दुर्विदग्ध badly learned",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "or wise, vain, arrogant ( with little learning; ज्ञानलवेन दुर्विदग्धः ).",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "दुर्विदग्धो दुश्चतुरः अर्धज्वलित इत्यर्थः । Rámarshi. Cf. Little know-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "ledge is a dangerous thing. ब्रह्मा-derived fr. बृह् 1. 6. P. to grow",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "+मनिन्, the ऋ being changed to र before it by Un. IV.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "145. रंजयति—रंज् cau. means to colour, to impart one’s hue",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "to : hence to win over, to gratify or propitiate. The cau. form",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "is रजयति when the meaning is to sport with or hunt deer;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "see Kir. VI. 24. Some read the line as ब्रह्मापि तं नरं &c. but this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "violates the laws of metre ( as it makes 17 mâtra's in the Pàda",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "instead of 15 or 18 ) and is therefore inadmissible.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 4. प्रसह्य—Indec., with great force. मणि from. मण् to sound",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "+इ ( न् ). मकर०-मं विषं किरतीति ( कॄ+अच् ) a crocodile, a shark.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "वक्त्र—वक्त्यनेनेति from वच्+ष्ट्रन् करणे. दंष्ट्रा-also der. with ष्ट्रन्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "from दंश् to bite. ०—अंकुर V. l.—from अंक् to mark, stamp+",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "उरच् , means pointed, sharp. दंष्ट्रांकुरात्-from the tips or points",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "( i. e when held fast between the points ) of the jaws; sing. for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "pl. Cf. दर्भांकुर S'ak, and दीपांकुर Vair. S'a 63. प्रचलदू०—ruffled or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "agitated with a series of rolling billows, ॰ऊर्मि m. f. from ऋ+मि,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "अर्तेरूच्च Un. IV. 44.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "भुजंगः—भुजः ( bent, curved कुटिलीभवन् ) सन् गच्छतीति; भुज्+",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "मुम्+खच्; मुम् ( the nasal ) inserted by ‘ अरुर्द्विषदजन्तस्य मुम् ’ Pân",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "VI. 3. 67.—Before the aff. खच् and खश् the words अरुस्, द्विषत्,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "and such as end in अ take the aug. म् when used preposi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "tionally with verbs. पुष्पवत्-पुष्पेण तुल्यम् like a flower. तेन तुल्यं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "क्रिया चेद्वतिः Pàn. V. I. 15. वत् is attached to a noun in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "sense of तेन तुल्यं ‘ equally with that ’ when the equality refers",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
